"NPDES 2022 Construction Stormwater General Permit | California State Water Resources Control Board (https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/water_issues/programs/stormwater/construction/general_permit_reissuance.html)\nciteturn1335view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view0\",\"id\":97}); Total lines: 568\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulation I - General Provisions (https://www.aqmd.gov/home/rules-compliance/rules/scaqmd-rule-book/regulation-i)\nciteturn1335view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1318view2\",\"id\":106}); Total lines: 258\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulation II - Permits (https://www.aqmd.gov/home/rules-compliance/rules/scaqmd-rule-book/regulation-ii)\nciteturn1335view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1318view2\",\"id\":107}); Total lines: 303\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulation III - Fees (https://www.aqmd.gov/home/rules-compliance/rules/scaqmd-rule-book/regulation-iii)\nciteturn1335view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1318view2\",\"id\":108}); Total lines: 330\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulation IV - Prohibitions (https://www.aqmd.gov/home/rules-compliance/rules/scaqmd-rule-book/regulation-iv)\nciteturn1335view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1318view2\",\"id\":109}); Total lines: 358\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegulation XI - Source Specific Standards (https://www.aqmd.gov/home/rules-compliance/rules/scaqmd-rule-book/regulation-xi)\nciteturn1335view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1318view2\",\"id\":114}); Total lines: 483\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNAUPAIICodes_2023_RS_2(GK).pub (https://www.sco.ca.gov/Files-UPD/upd_naupa_II_codes_dormancy_periods.pdf)\nciteturn1335view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view1\",\"pattern\":\"2023\"}); Total lines: 285\nNo matching text found for \"2023\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHolder Due Diligence (https://sco.ca.gov/Files-UPD/upd_duediligence.pdf)\nciteturn1335view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 3; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view2\",\"pattern\":\"Rev\"}); Total lines: 190\nNo matching text found for \"Rev\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRemitting Unclaimed Property to California (https://sco.ca.gov/Files-UPD/upd_remitting_property_factsheet.pdf)\nciteturn1335view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view4\",\"pattern\":\"Rev\"}); Total lines: 80\nL8@P0: Laws and Regulations and EFT Quick Guide for more details.\nL9@P0: Remitting Cash\nL10@P0: Any payment of unclaimed cash equaling $2,000 or more must be made by electronic fund transfer (EFT), per\nL11@P0: California Code of Civil Procedure (CCP) section 1532. Holders may remit payments under $2,000 either by EFT or\nL12@P0: by check payable to “California State Controller.” Any person who makes a payment of $2,000 or more by means\nL13@P0: other than EFT is liable for a civil penalty.\nL14@P0: All holders are encouraged to register for EFT by completing the Authorization Agreement and emailing it to the\nL15@P0: EFT Help Desk at UPDSCOEFT@sco.ca.gov. To ensure on-time remittance, establish new accounts before April 30.\nL16@P0:  The Controller’s Office offers a free web payment service only through the ACH Debit option at\nL17@P0: govone.com/PAYCAL.\nL18@P0:  When establishing an ACH Debit account, ensure it is the holder’s checking or savings account. Payments\nL19@P0: from a general ledger or trust account will be rejected.\nL20@P0:  If remitting by ACH Credit, confirm that the holder’s financial institution is able to originate an ACH Credit\nL21@P0: transaction in a CCD, PPD, or CXT file — the only formats accepted by the Controller’s Office.\nL22@P0: Prior to transferring funds for multiple reports in a single wire, email a list of Report ID numbers and\nL23@P0: the breakdown of funds to the EFT Help Desk, and include that list with the Remit Report.\nL24@P0: Rev. 4/2026\nL25@P0: We’re Here to Help!\nL26@P0: The OCU educates holders through webinars, speaking engagements,\nL27@P0: and more. Visit the trainings and tutorials page for up-to-date\nL28@P0: information or contact the OCU to schedule one-on-one assistance.\nL29@P0: GoReport.sco.ca.gov ● claimit.ca.gov\nL30@P0: Outreach and Compliance Unit\nL31@P0: (916) 464-6088\nL32@P0: UPDHolderOutreach@sco.ca.gov\nL33@P0: For additional assistance, contact the Controller’s team:\nL34@P0: Reporting Unit\nL35@P0: UCPReporting@sco.ca.gov\nL36@P0: (916) 464-6284\nL37@P0: EFT Help Desk\nL38@P0: UPDSCOEFT@sco.ca.gov\nL39@P0: (916) 464-6220\nL40@P0: Securities Management\nL41@P0: and Reconciliation\nL42@P0: UPDSecRecon@sco.ca.gov\nL43@P0-1: (916) 464-7123Remitting Unclaimed Property to California\nL44@P1: Remitting Securities\nL45@P1: Ensure the correct Committee on Uniform Securities Identification Procedures (CUSIP) numbers for all securities\nL46@P1: are identified on both the Remit Report and the Securities Summary form (SS-1).\nL47@P1: Account for any corporate actions that occurred after the Notice Report was submitted. An electronic transfer\nL48@P1: through the Depository Trust Company (DTC) is the most efficient method to deliver unclaimed securities.\nL49@P1: Summary Form\nL50@P1: Complete the SS-1 Securities Summary form to provide a list of security issues and file it with the Remit Report.\nL51@P1: Include the Report ID number in the form, and email the completed form to both the Controller’s broker at\nL52@P1: Calif.StateMail@wellsfargoadvisors.com and the Controller’s Financial Accounting and Reporting Unit at\nL53@P1: UCPDTCSS1@sco.ca.gov. Include a copy of the SS-1 with the DTC receipt confirmations when submitting your\nL54@P1: Remit Report to the Controller’s Office.\nL55@P1: Whole and Fractional Shares\nL56@P1: Whole reported shares in individual stock owner accounts should be transferred to the Controller’s contracted\nL57@P1: broker via DTC, or certificated after each owner’s account is converted to whole shares and registered in the\nL58@P1: name of the State Controller. Liquidate fractional shares and remit in cash.\nL59@P1: Dividends in Cash\nL60@P1: The Controller does not participate in dividend reinvestment plans (DRIPs). Prior to escheating properties,\nL61@P1: terminate all established DRIPs and replace them with cash dividend options. Remit all dividend earnings in cash.\nL62@P1: Non-Transferrable Securities\nL63@P1: California law does not exclude worthless or non-transferrable securities from reporting requirements. Contact\nL64@P1: the Controller’s contracted broker to determine if securities are deemed non-transferrable and, if so, include the\nL65@P1: broker’s written verification with the Remit Report.\nL66@P1: Remitting Safekeeping Property\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUniversal Holder Face Sheet (https://www.sco.ca.gov/Files-UPD/form_rptg_ufs-1.pdf)\nciteturn1335view9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 3; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view5\",\"pattern\":\"Rev\"}); Total lines: 134\nL0@P0: State of California—Controller’s Office\nL1@P0: UNIVERSAL HOLDER FACE SHEET (must be completed and submitted with all reports)\nL2@P0: UFS-1(Rev. 04/2024)\nL3@P0: Upload to the online Holder Reporting Portal with all other required reporting materials.\nL4@P0: Notice Report Remit Report\nL5@P0: Report ID# (Remit Report Only)\nL6@P0: Required\nL7@P0: Section A—Holder Information\nL8@P0: FEIN Branch Number Report As of Date Check Number / EFT Debit Ref Number (Remit Report Only)\nL9@P0:  Or\nL10@P0: Section B—Holder Contact Information Holder Name\nL11@P0: Street Address\nL12@P0: P.O. Box Number City State Zip Code Country\nL13@P0: Contact Name (For report completion) Title Phone Number Extension\nL14@P0: E-mail Address\nL15@P0: Section C—Property Owner Contact Information Holder Name\nL16@P0: Street Address\nL17@P0: P.O. Box Number City State Zip Code Country\nL18@P0: Contact Name Title Phone Number Extension\nL19@P0: E-mail Address\nL20@P0: Section D—Holder Agent Contact (If Applicable) Agent Name\nL21@P0: City State Zip Code Country\nL22@P0: Contact Name (For report completion) Title Phone Number Extension\nL23@P0: Street Address\nL24@P0: P.O. Box Number\nL25@P0: E-mail Address\nL26@P0: Section E—Holder CEO/CFO Name Title\nL27@P0: Address\nL28@P0: P.O. Box Number City State Zip Code Country\nL29@P0: Total Reported/Remitted Shares\nL30@P0: *Any Remittance of $2,000 or more must be paid by Electronic Funds Transfer (EFT), pursuant to Code of Civil Procedures (CCP) Section 1532.\nL31@P0: Section F—Holder Report Totals Total Reported/Remitted Dollars Includes Safe Deposit Box\nL32@P0:   Yes No\nL33@P0: Section G—Holder Business Information\nL34@P0: Organization Type: NAICS Code:\nL35@P0: Incorporation State: Incorporation Date : / / Charter Federal  or State  Charter Date: / /\nL36@P0: Agent Name\nL37@P0: Section H—Demutualization Proceeds This report includes proceeds from the demutualization of an insurance company.\nL38@P0: Section I—Transfer Agent (If Applicable)\nL39@P0: Street Address\nL40@P0: P.O. Box Number City State Zip Code Country\nL41@P0: Section J—Verification\nL42@P0: Section J - Verification If made by an individual, shall be verified by the individual; if made by a partnership, by a partner; if made by an unincorporated association or\nL43@P0: private corporation, by an officer; if made by a public corporation, by its chief fiscal officer or other employee authorized by the holder (CCP Section 1530(e)).\nL44@P0: The undersigned, declares, under penalty of perjury, that, to the best of (his) (her) knowledge and belief, the following sheets\nL45@P0: contain a full, true, and complete report of unclaimed property which is presumed unclaimed under the provisions of Part 3, Title 10, Chapter 7, Code of Civil Procedure,\nL46@P0: commencing with Section 1500, and Title 2, California Administrative Code, Sections 1150 et seq. The Undersigned also confirms that all properties not listed on the\nL47@P0: Remit Report, which were initially included on the Notice Report, were not remitted due to contact by the apparent owner, or the property being reactivated\nL48@P0: or returned to the rightful owner.\nL49@P0: Signature Title Date\nL50@P0: UFS-1 (Rev 4/24)\nL51@P0: Date of Demutualization CCP Section 1515.5 (a) CCP Section 1515.5 (b) CCP Section 1515.5 (c)\nL52@P0: Due Between June 1 and June 15\nL53@P0: Life Insurance Due Between December 1 and December 15\nL54@P0: Voluntary Compliance Program (See 14F Remit Reminder Letter for due date)\nL55@P0: Due Before November 1\nL56@P0: Life Insurance Due Before May 1\nL57@P0: Voluntary Compliance Program (See form SCO VCP 02 for due date)\nL58@P0: Supplemental Notice Report (For reports with properties that should have been but were not included in the previously submitted Notice Report)\nL59@P0: |\nL60@P0-1: E-mail AddressUniversal Holder Face Sheet Instructions\nL61@P1: The Universal Holder Face Sheet (UFS-1) form must be completed and submitted with all reports.\nL62@P1: Notice Report: Check this box when submitting a Notice Report. This report is due annually prior to\nL63@P1: November 1 or prior to May 1 for life insurance companies. Participants in the Voluntary Compliance\nL64@P1: Program (VCP) have alternate due dates specified in the VCP Requirements (SCO VCP 02) form. If the\nL65@P1: holder identifies accounts that were not included on the original Notice Report, they must be reported on\nL66@P1: a separate Supplemental Notice Report and must not be included on the Remit Report.\nL67@P1: Remit Report: Check this box when submitting a Remit Report. This report is due between June 1-15 or\nL68@P1: between December 1-15 for life insurance companies. Participants in the VCP have alternate due dates\nL69@P1: specified in the SCO VCP 02 form. All holders, including those enrolled in the VCP, should refer to the\nL70@P1: 14F Remit Reminder Letter to confirm when the Remit Report is due.\nL71@P1: Voluntary Compliance Program: Check the VCP box only if the report is being submitted during the\nL72@P1: time frame assigned upon enrollment into the VCP and includes past-due property for which interest is\nL73@P1: requested to be waived. Participants in the VCP have alternate due dates specified in the SCO VCP 02\nL74@P1: form.\nL75@P1: Supplemental Notice Report: Check this box when submitting a Supplemental Notice Report, for\nL76@P1: holders who have identified accounts that were not included on the original Notice Report.\nL77@P1: Report ID# (Remit Report Only): List the Remit Report ID number located on the upper right-hand\nL78@P1: corner of the Remit Reminder Letter (14F). If you did not receive a 14F letter, contact the Reporting Unit\nL79@P1: at 916-464-6284 for assistance. For Remit Reports, also include the EFT debit reference number or\nL80@P1: check number.\nL81@P1: Section A - Holder Information: Provide the Federal Employer Identification Number (FEIN), branch\nL82@P1: number (if applicable), report “As of” date, and check number/EFT debit reference number. The FEIN\nL83@P1: and report “As of” date are required. Failure to provide this information will result in the report being\nL84@P1: rejected.\nL85@P1: FEIN: Enter the FEIN number.\nL86@P1: Branch Number: Enter the branch number, if applicable.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.sco.ca.gov/Files-UPD/form_rptg_hcr-1.pdf)\nciteturn1335view10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1325view6\",\"pattern\":\"Rev\"}); Total lines: 187\nNo matching text found for \"Rev\""
